diff --git a/apps/gallery/docs/CANONICAL-IMPORT.md b/apps/gallery/docs/CANONICAL-IMPORT.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a7fba84
--- /dev/null
+++ b/apps/gallery/docs/CANONICAL-IMPORT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# Canonical catalogue import
+
+Gallery imports canonical records; it does not infer canonical identity from a selected filename, path, content URI, provider ID, or UI record.
+
+## Accepted JSON
+
+The importer accepts either:
+
+1. one pinned `asset-record` v1 object; or
+2. a `gallery-canonical-import` v1 envelope containing `assets`, `source_occurrences`, and optional bounded `metadata` arrays.
+
+Every asset must be `ready`, use a lowercase `sha256:<64 hex>` `asset_id`, and have an identical `content_hash`. Every occurrence must use the pinned source-occurrence v1 shape and refer to an asset in the same batch. Duplicate asset IDs, occurrence IDs, metadata records, and orphan references are rejected before merge.
+
+The envelope is a Gallery adapter around the pinned records, not a replacement for an Extract-owned collection contract. `contracts/source.json` identifies the pinned source snapshot.
+
+## Limits and presentation metadata
+
+The UTF-8 JSON input is limited to 10 MiB. A bundle accepts at most 20,000 assets, 100,000 occurrences, and 20,000 metadata entries. Titles, tags, descriptions, OCR text, and an embedded image preview are separately bounded.
+
+Preview data may only use a bounded `data:image/png`, `data:image/jpeg`, or `data:image/webp` base64 URI. Filesystem paths and remote HTTP(S) preview URLs are rejected. Imported presentation metadata is non-authoritative and never changes `asset_id` or source provenance.
+
+## Locator safety
+
+`storage_locator`, `source_location`, `original_path`, archive locations, and source members are retained only as canonical/provenance metadata. The mobile importer never opens, fetches, or copies those values. Selecting the JSON grants access only to that selected JSON file, not to an Extract host path or source original.
+
+## Atomic merge and Gallery state
+
+The merge validates the complete batch before returning a new normalized snapshot. Assets are keyed by `asset_id`; occurrences are keyed by `source_occurrence_id`. Reimport is idempotent, new occurrences for existing bytes are retained, and conflicting canonical size/MIME/hash or occurrence provenance rejects the whole batch without mutating the current snapshot.
+
+Gallery annotations—including review state, notes, preferred occurrence/copy, labels, and presentation choices—remain separate from canonical and source records. Existing annotations survive reimport. A previously stored embedded preview survives when a later import omits preview data. Output asset, occurrence, and Analysis-view ordering is deterministic.
